.TH "LINTO-COMPLETION" 1

.SH "Shell completion and Markdown navigation"
.PP
Linto includes Bash, Zsh, and Fish completion definitions\. Ask the dispatcher
for the setup instruction for your shell:
.RS
.PP
.nf
linto completion bash
linto completion zsh
linto completion fish
.fi
.RE
.PP
For Zsh, add the printed \fBfpath\fP setup and \fBcompinit\fP line to your Zsh startup
configuration (normally \fB~/\.zshrc\fP), or run \fBlinto\-linto\-setup\fP to configure a
supported shell automatically\. Restart the shell or source the updated
configuration\. Fish completion is optional; it is not required for Linto or for
Bash/Zsh completion\.

.SS "Navigating with mdless"
.PP
If \fBmdless\fP is installed and comes before other installed viewers in the
\fBmarkdown\-viewer\fP preference list, it will be selected to display guide pages\.
Use these keys while viewing a page:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
\fBj\fP/\fBk\fP or the arrow keys to scroll\.
.IP \(bu 4
Space or \fBf\fP to page down; \fBb\fP to page up\.
.IP \(bu 4
\fB/\fP to search; \fBn\fP/\fBN\fP to move between matches\.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBg\fP/\fBG\fP to jump to the beginning/end\.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBq\fP to quit; \fBh\fP to open \fBmdless\fP's built\-in help\.
.RE
